#!/bin/sh
# setup — make ai-usage-statusline Claude Code's status line, in
# ~/.claude/settings.json (a copy of it is kept first). A status line of
# your own is kept, and runs through it: its line is still the one you see.
set -eu
settings="$HOME/.claude/settings.json"
own_dir="${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/vikix/plugins/ai-usage"
mkdir -p "$HOME/.claude" "$own_dir"
[ -e "$settings" ] && cp -p "$settings" "$settings.vikix-bak.$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)"
python3 - "$settings" "$HOME/.local/bin/ai-usage-statusline" "$own_dir/your-statusline" <<'PY'
import json, os, sys
path, ours, keep = sys.argv[1:4]
try:
    with open(path) as f:
        settings = json.load(f)
except FileNotFoundError:
    settings = {}
line = settings.get("statusLine") or {}
command = line.get("command", "") if isinstance(line, dict) else ""
if command and command != ours:
    with open(keep, "w") as f:      # yours, run through ours from now on
        f.write(command + "\n")
settings["statusLine"] = {"type": "command", "command": ours}
tmp = path + ".vikix-new"
with open(tmp, "w") as f:
    json.dump(settings, f, indent=2)
    f.write("\n")
os.replace(tmp, path)
PY
echo "   Claude Code's status line now notes your plan's use: sessions started from now on show it (a running one, once restarted)"
